> shneg(x: i8 in -128..-1) = -x << 1
> wrap shneg
wrap analysis of shneg:
  -x   (i8)
      nuw fails: unsigned wrap at 128 points, e.g. x=-128
      nsw fails: signed wrap at 1 points, e.g. x=-128  <- UB in C; a compiler assumes it cannot happen
  -x << 1   (i8)
      nuw fails: unsigned wrap at 1 points, e.g. x=-128
      nsw fails: signed wrap at 65 points, e.g. x=-128  <- UB in C; a compiler assumes it cannot happen
  end to end: differs from the mathematical result at 65 points, e.g. x=-128
      exact for: -63..-1
  over all 128 points of the domain
> shr(x: i8) = x >> 1
> wrap shr
wrap analysis of shr:
  no wrapping or rounding operations
  end to end: equals the mathematical (unbounded) result everywhere
  over all 256 points of the domain
> range shr
range of shr -> i8:
  -64..63   (128 distinct values)
  fits in i7
  over all 256 points of the domain
